{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New Jersey security deposit maximum and annual increase cap","requirement":"A landlord may not take a security deposit above 1.5 times one month’s rent, may not raise it over 10% a year, and at lease start may require no more than 2.5 times the monthly rent including first month’s rent.","key_value":"1.5 times one month’s rent; annual increase max 10%","coverage_conditions":"Residential rentals in New Jersey; the guide states no building-type, age or unit-count limit on the cap.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2","quoted_span":"The maximum-security deposit to be collected by the landlord cannot be more than one and one-half times one month’s rent (N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.2). It can be less. Any additional yearly security deposit increase may not exceed 10% of the current security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit interest belongs to the tenant","requirement":"Interest or earnings on a security deposit belong to the tenant and must be paid in cash or credited to rent on the lease renewal or anniversary, or on January 31 if the landlord gave written notice of that payment date.","key_value":"interest paid annually to tenant","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19","quoted_span":"The interest or earnings paid on the security deposit belongs to the tenant and shall be paid to the tenant in cash or credited toward rent due and owing on the renewal or anniversary of the tenant’s lease or on January 31, if the tenant has been given written notice, that the interest payments will be paid on January 31 of each year","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit notice and 7% tenant remedy","requirement":"Within 30 days of receiving a deposit, and each year, a landlord must notify the tenant of the bank, amount, account type and rate. If notice or interest is not given, the tenant may apply the deposit plus 7% interest per year to rent.","key_value":"notice within 30 days; 7% per annum remedy","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-19.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days of receipt of the security deposit and at the time of each annual interest payment, the landlord must notify the tenant in writing of the name and address of the banking institution or investment company in which the money is deposited, the amount of the deposit, type of account, and current rate of interest for the account.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return deadline and double-damages penalty","requirement":"Within 30 days after a tenancy ends — 5 business days if the tenant is displaced by fire, flood, condemnation or evacuation — a landlord must return the deposit plus interest less itemized deductions; failure can mean double damages.","key_value":"30 days (5 business days if displaced); double damages","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies in New Jersey; for a broken lease the 30 days runs from re-rental or lease expiration, whichever is first.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Double the amount wrongfully withheld, plus court costs and reasonable attorney’s fees.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"Within 30 days after the termination of a tenancy, a landlord must return the security deposit, plus interest earned less deductions, to the tenant (N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-01","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Security deposit return after Safe Housing Act termination","requirement":"When a tenant ends a lease under the Safe Housing Act, the landlord must make the security deposit plus interest available for return within 15 business days after termination, and notify the tenant within 3 business days where to collect it.","key_value":"15 business days","coverage_conditions":"Tenancies ended by a domestic violence victim under the New Jersey Safe Housing Act.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Safe Housing Act lease terminations"},"exemptions":"Transient or seasonal rentals.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-9.6","quoted_span":"Within 15 business days after the lease is terminated, the landlord shall make available the return of the tenant’s security deposit, plus any interest earned, to the tenant or the tenant’s agent.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
